## ternary operator
it can be used to replace multiple lines of code with a single line. It is often used to replace simple if else statements
Syntax:
```
variable = (condition) ? expressionTrue : expressionFalse
```

For example:
```C#
double temp = 25;
string result = (temp <= 25) ? "good temp" : "bad temp";
Console.WriteLine(result) // if temp <= 25, outputs good temo, else outputs bad temp.
```

## switch statements
use the switch statement to select one of many code blocks to be executed
this is the skeleton of the switch statement:
```C#
switch(object){
    case condition1:
        statement;
        break; // break keyword is used for breaking out of the switch statement
    case condition2:
        statement;
        break; 
    default:  // default is used for the case when there's no case can be matched
        statement;
        break;
}
```
